From 05beb5ef1d96790f60ae5df21e2dea97ad452577 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 01:19:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove hardcoded fallback content - nothing shows on the
 frontend that doesn't exist in the backend

Reported bug: the writer deleted the default seeded Impact Stories, and
they kept showing up on novessafoundation.org.ng anyway. Root cause: the
content API (list_content, content_detail, site_payload) has always merged
real published content with hardcoded demo defaults from defaults.py -
for any of the original 6 programs/6 stories/1 campaign/4 partners, if no
matching published database row existed (never created, deleted, or just
unpublished), the API silently fell back to the original seed text
instead of omitting it. There was no way to actually remove one of these
by deleting or unpublishing it - the system was architecturally incapable
of it.

Fix: content/views.py no longer merges anything. list_content and
site_payload return only what is actually published in the database.
content_detail 404s instead of returning fallback text for anything not
published. Applied identically across all four content types (programs,
stories, campaigns, partners), per the explicit instruction that this
should be consistent everywhere, not just stories.

Also fixed a related instance of the same category of bug found while
investigating: the donate page and the donation-creation endpoint both
hardcoded 'community-care-fund' as a fallback campaign slug - meaning a
donation could get silently tagged to a campaign that no longer exists.
Both now fall back to a neutral 'general' value instead of naming a
specific campaign that may not be real.

Scope note: SiteSetting (homepage_hero/site_summary) fallback behavior is
intentionally left as-is - that's global site configuration a developer
sets up once, not a list of deletable content items, and is a different
concern from the reported bug. Happy to remove that too if wanted.

Frontend: added graceful 'nothing published yet' empty states to
/programs, /blog, and /partners for when a content type has zero
published items, instead of a silently blank section.

Tests: rewrote the three existing tests that asserted the old fallback
behavior to assert the new correct behavior instead, and added a new test
covering the exact reported scenario (deleting everything empties all
four content types on the frontend).

Verified extensively given the scope of this change: manage.py check,
ruff, black clean. Directly executed all 6 test scenarios against the
real database (including the exact client-reported scenario). Then ran a
full local integration test - real Django backend + real built Next.js
frontend served together - confirming: (1) with an empty database, every
affected page returns 200 and shows the new empty-state text, not a
crash; (2) the donate page correctly sends 'general' instead of the old
hardcoded campaign slug; (3) after re-seeding real content, every page
still displays it completely normally - no regression.
